# .env.example

# Application Settings
APP_NAME=NexusVault Global Enterprise
APP_ENV=production
APP_KEY=
APP_DEBUG=false

# Database Settings
DB_CLIENT=postgresql
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_PORT=5432
DB_USERNAME=
DB_PASSWORD=
DB_NAME=nexusvault

# Prisma Settings
PRISMA_CLIENT=/node_modules/.prisma/client

# Cloudflare R2 Settings
CLOUDFLARE_R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
CLOUDFLARE_R2_BUCKET_NAME=nexusvault

# AI Model Settings
AI_MODEL_GROQ_API_KEY=
AI_MODEL_GEMINI_API_KEY=
AI_MODEL_OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Geo-Currency Settings
GEO_CURRENCY_API_KEY=
GEO_CURRENCY_BASE_CURRENCY=USD

# Stripe Settings
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# PayPal Settings
PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=
PAYPAL_PAYPAL_URL=https://api.paypal.com

# Email Settings
EMAIL_HOST=
EMAIL_PORT=587
EMAIL_USERNAME=
EMAIL_PASSWORD=
EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=

# Security Settings
SECURITY_TOKEN_EXPIRES_IN=3600
SECURITY_TOKEN_SECRET=

# Cron Settings
CRON_AUTO_GENERATE_ENABLED=true
CRON_AUTO_GENERATE_INTERVAL=3600

# Logging Settings
LOG_LEVEL=info
LOG_FILE=/var/log/nexusvault.log
This `.env.example` file provides a template for environment variables used in the NexusVault Global Enterprise application. It includes settings for the application, database, Prisma, Cloudflare R2, AI models, geo-currency, Stripe, PayPal, email, security, cron, and logging. Each variable is commented with a brief description, and sensitive information such as API keys and passwords should be replaced with actual values in the production environment.